{
  "name": "Gmail triage with Hesperan (Auto or Review)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Gmail triage with Hesperan\n\n**Who it's for:** teams working from one Gmail inbox who sort mail with labels.\n\n**What it does:** each new email goes to a calibrated Hesperan decision profile. On **Auto** (the calibrated confidence reached the profile's threshold) it gets the team's label. On **Review** it gets a *Needs review* label, and a person decides.\n\n**Setup**\n1. In the Hesperan console, create and calibrate a profile (here `mail-routing`) with one answer per team.\n2. Add credentials: Hesperan (API key `hsp_…`) and Gmail (OAuth2).\n3. Replace the label IDs `Label_…` in both Gmail nodes with yours (a Gmail node with *Label → Get Many* lists them).\n\nRe-runs are safe: the Gmail message ID is the Idempotency-Key, so the same email within 24 hours returns the first decision and is not charged twice.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "e595e3af-b0d3-5324-b90f-d104f79e1bdc",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -600,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Auto\nLabel with the team the profile chose.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b8e7bf21-a767-5116-ad1b-2932e5d46550",
      "name": "Auto section",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Review\nLabel for a person to decide.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 3
      },
